  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Qataris carry their own name, bin (son of) or bint (daughter of) their father's name, often the grandfather's, then the family or tribal name with Al, as in Hamad bin Jassim Al Kuwari or Noora bint Khalid Al Marri. Day to day it is the first name and the family name, and women keep their own family name after marriage. Most people in Qatar come from abroad and keep their home conventions: Keralites use a house name, caste name or the father's name; Nepalis use a family name tied to their community, such as Gurung, Tamang or Shrestha; Bangladeshis often carry a second name like Hossain or Rahman rather than a fixed surname; Filipinos have Spanish family names with English or double first names like Mary Grace. People call each other by first name with a title such as Bhai, Dai, Chetta or Kabayan.",
